From: csdivad <csdivad@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] winepulse: provide the stream-state helpers the media rework
 calls

The media-rework patches call pulse_stream_ready() and pulse_stream_haptic(),
but both helpers were defined by the removed proton-ds5-haptic series, so
winepulse failed with implicit declarations (pulse.c:1355, 1914) and an
unused-function error for pulse_cond_timedwait_ms.

Define them with upstream-equivalent semantics - "ready" means the PA stream
exists and is READY, "haptic" is always FALSE because there is no DualSense
routing any more - and mark the now-unused condition-variable helper.

Fork-local: keeps the wine media-rework stack building without DualSense support.
---
--- a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
+++ b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
@@ -179,7 +179,7 @@
     return pthread_cond_wait(&pulse_cond, &pulse_mutex);
 }
 
-static int pulse_cond_timedwait_ms(unsigned int timeout_ms)
+static int __attribute__((unused)) pulse_cond_timedwait_ms(unsigned int timeout_ms)
 {
     struct timespec ts;
 
@@ -493,6 +493,17 @@
     return pa_stream_get_state(stream->stream) == PA_STREAM_READY;
 }
 
+/* No DualSense stack: the media-rework patches still call these helpers. */
+static BOOL pulse_stream_ready(struct pulse_stream *stream)
+{
+    return stream && stream->stream && pa_stream_get_state(stream->stream) == PA_STREAM_READY;
+}
+
+static BOOL pulse_stream_haptic(struct pulse_stream *stream)
+{
+    return FALSE;
+}
+
 static HRESULT pulse_connect(const char *name)
 {
     pa_context_state_t state;
